            <ArticleTitle>Adjuncts should always be used in pediatric regional anesthesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>100-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/pan.12526</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A number of different adjuncts to local anesthetics can be used to prolong and optimize postoperative pain relief following regional anesthesia in children. The present text provides a slightly opinionated but evidence-based argument in favor of this practice.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2014 John Wiley &amp; Sons Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
